1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,463
Temperature is not the only thing that changes the clock.

2
00:00:03,463 --> 00:00:04,466
Light can too.

3
00:00:04,466 --> 00:00:07,187
A peptide is a chain of amino acids.

4
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:11,614
Some of those links can absorb light, especially ultraviolet light.

5
00:00:11,614 --> 00:00:14,375
Tryptophan and tyrosine are two of them.

6
00:00:14,375 --> 00:00:18,111
When they absorb that energy, the molecule can oxidize.

7
00:00:18,111 --> 00:00:21,927
The chain looks the same in the vial, but part of it has changed.

8
00:00:21,927 --> 00:00:24,856
Not every peptide is equally sensitive.

9
00:00:24,856 --> 00:00:26,588
It depends on the sequence.

10
00:00:26,588 --> 00:00:30,677
Stay tuned to learn which chains are more sensitive, and which are less.

11
00:00:30,677 --> 00:00:34,023
That is why many peptide labels say protect from light.

12
00:00:34,023 --> 00:00:36,041
The box is not decoration.

13
00:00:36,041 --> 00:00:38,281
It is part of the storage instructions.

14
00:00:38,281 --> 00:00:40,364
Light is a clock you cannot see.

15
00:00:40,364 --> 00:00:41,692
Day six of ten.

16
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:43,750
Follow so you don't miss day seven.

